<title>CANADA: Kinross sees 1997 output dropping.</title>
<headline>Kinross sees 1997 output dropping.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kinross Gold Corp said on Thursday it expected its 1997 gold equivalent production to drop three percent from 1996 to about 510,000 ounces after rock bursts damaged part of its Kirkland Lake, Ontario, mine.</p>
<p>Its Macassa mine was now forecast to produce 55,000 ounces of gold instead of 91,000 ounces, Kinross said.</p>
<p>Macassa cash operating costs were seen rising to about US$350 an ounce of gold this year, about US$100 an ounce above its original estimate.</p>
<p>A series of rock bursts damaged Macassa's number three shaft on April 12.</p>
</text>
